\section*{Margulis–Platonov normal-subgroup conjecture}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 018; 2026-09-23), the asserted result is that the corresponding normal-subgroup description holds over number fields using the anisotropic nonarchimedean local groups.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 018; 2026-09-23), commuting approximation with prescribed determinants reduces the remaining unitary cases to finite quotients and local abelianization. Metaplectic splitting, recurrence, and explicit root involutions eliminate residual characters, while finite-group tests rule out the remaining simple quotients.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 018; 2026-09-23).

